<div class="shell">
<h2 id="transports-heading">Your agent, in your chat.</h2>
<p>Slack's classic profile works on free workspaces; its Agent profile adds native status where enabled. Each service has its own progress controls.</p>
<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Chat service comparison">
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Chat service</th>
<th scope="col">Conversation</th>
<th scope="col">Progress</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Slack</th>
<td data-label="Conversation">DMs, mentions and opted-in thread follow</td>
<td data-label="Progress">Classic reactions or progress; Agent Working/Stop status</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Discord</th>
<td data-label="Conversation">DMs, server mentions and opted-in follow</td>
<td data-label="Progress">Typing; optional streamed edits and Stop button</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">WhatsApp</th>
<td data-label="Conversation">Individual chats</td>
<td data-label="Progress">Typing; no streaming</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Telegram</th>
<td data-label="Conversation">DMs and addressed groups/topics</td>
<td data-label="Progress">Typing; optional streamed edits and Stop button</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Configured journals retain conversation records and attachment references across restarts. Journal replay can use background summaries; platform recall reads available chat history instead. Image understanding needs a compatible model, and file replies need a provider plus a delivery grant. <a href="/how-it-works/#memory">Memory settings</a> · <a href="/deploy/mac/">Connect Slack on a Mac</a>.</p>
